DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     This function determines if a subject with credential _u_1 can see a sub‐
     ject or object associated to credential _u_2.

     Specific types of subjects may need to submit to additional or different
     restrictions.  As an example, for processes, see p_cansee(9), which calls
     this function.

     The implementation relies on cr_bsd_visible(9) and consequently the
     sysctl(8) variables referenced in its manual page influence the result.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     This function returns zero if the subject with credential _u_1 can “see”
     the subject or object with credential _u_2, or ESRCH otherwise.

EERRRROORRSS
     [ESRCH]            The subject with credential _u_1 has been jailed and the
                        subject or object with credential _u_2 does not belong
                        to the same jail or one of its sub-jails, as deter‐
                        mined by prison_check(9).

     [ESRCH]            The MAC subsystem denied visibility.

     [ESRCH]            cr_bsd_visible(9) denied visibility according to the
                        BSD security policies in force.

